<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb green coffee imports rise 18.8 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb green coffee imports rise 18.8 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's green coffee imports in February totalled 27,397 tonnes, up by 18.8 percent from the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Friday showed.</p>
<p>Imports of roasted coffee amounted to 280 tonnes in February against 145 tonnes the same month a year earlier.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of green coffee imports (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   Feb 97	   Jan 97	   Feb 96</p>
<p> Total	   27,397	   27,431	   23,071</p>
<p> Brazil	   6,470	    6,231	    4,375</p>
<p> Colombia	 5,007	    6,408	    6,196</p>
<p> Indonesia	4,638	    4,281	    4,306</p>
<p> Honduras	 2,280	    1,494		840</p>
<p> Guatemala	2,170	    2,116	    1,074</p>
<p> Vietnam	  1,456	    1,155	    1,051</p>
<p> Mexico	   1,172	    1,033		345</p>
<p>Total green coffee imports in the first two months of 1997 were 54,828 tonnes, against 43,560 tonnes in the previous year.</p>
<p>Roasted coffee imports (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Feb 97	  Jan 97	   Feb 96</p>
<p> Total		280	     266		145</p>
<p>Cumulative roasted coffee imports in the first two months of 1997 were 546 tonnes against 291 a year before.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
